# Unsafe Parsing & Deserialization Reviewer Rule v1.0 STRICT

**Do not inline-audit.** Invoke **`unsafe_parsing_deserialization_reviewer`** -> `.cursor/agents/unsafe_parsing_deserialization_reviewer.md`.

## References

| Artifact | Path |
|---|---|
| Policy | `.cursor/skills/unsafe_parsing_deserialization_reviewer/POLICY.md` |
| Scan skill | `.cursor/skills/unsafe_parsing_deserialization_reviewer/SKILL.md` |
| Report path | `AI/unsafe_parsing_deserialization_reviewer/unsafe_parsing_deserialization_reviewer_report.md` |
| Report line | `unsafe_parsing_deserialization_reviewer v1.0 STRICT` |

**POLICY.md wins.**

## Invoke when

Use before deploy or when `ObjectInputStream`, XML parsing logic, Jackson/YAML polymorphic settings, zip extraction, or complex document parsing features (PDF, SVG, Office) change.

Skip for generated output, `target/`, `node_modules/`, and docs-only edits unless the docs define data processing or deserialization policy.

## Non-negotiable rules

1. **Native Java deserialization (`ObjectInputStream`) on untrusted data is always FAIL.**
2. **XML parsers instantiated without disabling external entities and DTDs is always FAIL.**
3. **Extracting zip entries to the filesystem without canonical path validation is always FAIL.**

## Finding table

Every finding includes:

| Row | Content |
|---|---|
| Evidence | Bad line or runtime proof from project |
| Policy Rule | POLICY.md - CHECK-ID - citation |
| Pattern | SKILL.md section 8 pattern |
| Mechanism | Plain English + framework/API names |
| Security property | What must be true after fix |
| Prohibited | Short label only |
| Verify | Action + pass signal |

Allowed verdicts: **PASS**, **FAIL**, **MANUAL_REVIEW**, **N/A**. `UNCLEAR` is forbidden.
